# The committed test vectors, their source files and the fuzz seeds are
# bytes, not text. Without this, Git classifies any of them that happens to
# contain no NUL byte as text and rewrites its line endings on checkout
# wherever `core.autocrlf` is on — which is the default on Windows. A vector
# that has been rewritten no longer matches what the decoder produces, and
# every differential test over it fails for a reason that has nothing to do
# with the decoder.
tests/data/** binary
fuzz/corpus/**/*.seed binary
